    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n**Open Viewing Times**\nMonday 5th October 4.00pm - 4.30pm.\nFriday 9th October 3.30pm - 4.00pm.\n\nWelcome to No. 21 Senandale, a spacious five bedroom detached residence occupying a generous corner site within a small and mature residential development.\n\nOverlooking a large green area, this wonderful home enjoys a peaceful setting while offering exceptional convenience, making it an ideal choice for growing families seeking space, comfort and a well established neighbourhood.\n\nThe ground floor accommodation comprises a glazed entrance porch leading into a bright and welcoming hallway. A large dual aspect living and dining room spans the width of the home, creating an excellent space for both everyday family living and entertaining. This room provides direct access to a well appointed kitchen located to the rear. A utility room offers convenient access to the rear garden and patio, while a family bathroom and a versatile sitting room/fifth bedroom completes the ground floor accommodation. Upstairs, there are four generously proportioned bedrooms, all featuring built-in wardrobes, together with a family bathroom.\n\nExternally, the property enjoys off street parking to the front, bordered by mature hedging, planting and attractive shrubbery. A gated side entrance leads to a private and enclosed rear garden featuring a patio area and lawn, ideal for outdoor dining, relaxation and family enjoyment. A block built garage to the side provides valuable additional storage space.\n\nIdeally positioned in the sought-after village of Cloghroe, this home offers the perfect balance of rural charm and everyday convenience. Cloghroe National School and an excellent range of local amenities, including a shop, church, post office, gym, hairdresser and beauty salon are all within a few minutes' walk of the property. A regular bus services, no.215, is located within a 5 minute stroll of the home and operates every 30 minutes to the city centre.\n\nFor sports and outdoor enthusiasts, Muskerry Golf Club is located less than 1km away, while Ballyanly Sportsgrounds, Ballincollig Regional Park and the scenic Inniscarra Lake are all within a short drive. The location also benefits from excellent road connectivity, with Ballincollig and Blarney reachable in approximately 10 minutes and Cork City just 15 minutes away.\n\nThis is a superb opportunity to acquire a spacious family home in a mature and highly convenient location.\n\nViewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nPorch - \nThe entrance porch features sliding glass doors and a large window overlooking the garden. The area is finished with a tiled floor.\n\nEntrance Hall - \nThe entrance hall is accessed through a glazed door and features tiled flooring, a staircase with wrought iron spindles, understairs storage, fitted alarm system and a convenient cloakroom.\n\nLiving Dining Room - 8.24m x 4.53m\nA superb dual aspect living and dining room accessed from both the entrance hall and kitchen, enjoying views over the front green and rear garden. Wood flooring, fitted shelving, Venetian blinds and a centre rose all add a touch of elegance, while a marble hearth and surround with electric insert stove provides a warm and inviting focal point.\n\nKitchen - 4.02m x 3.34m\nA well-appointed kitchen fitted with a comprehensive range of floor and eye-level units incorporating a stainless steel sink, four plate hob, extractor and oven, complemented by a tiled splashback and tiled flooring. A large window overlooking the rear garden and patio fills the space with natural light.\n\nSitting Room/ Bed 5 - 4.90m x 3.07m\nA versatile dual aspect room with wood flooring, Venetian blinds and fitted storage, featuring large windows overlooking the green and a glazed door providing direct access to the front garden.\n\nBathroom - 2.34m x 1.99m\nA fully tiled three piece shower suite with Mira attachment and recessed lighting.\n\nUtility & Rear Hall - \nA practical utility room with tiled flooring, plumbed for washer and dryer, with a glazed door providing direct access to the rear garden.\n\nFirst Floor - \n\n\nLanding - \nA bright and spacious landing providing access to all four bedrooms, bathroom and hotpress.\n\nBedroom 1 - 4.04m x 3.70m\nA generous double bedroom with wood flooring, Venetian blinds and a large window overlooking the front green, complemented by a double built-in wardrobe.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.69m x 3.38m\nA well-proportioned double bedroom with carpet flooring, Venetian blinds, a double built-in wardrobe and a window overlooking the rear garden and patio.\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.67m x 2.63m\nA single bedroom with carpet flooring, Venetian blinds and the benefit of built-in storage and fitted shelving.\n\nBedroom 4 - 3.56m x 2.30m\nA single bedroom to the rear with carpet flooring, Venetian blinds and a double built-in wardrobe.\n\nBathroom - 2.24m x 2.02m\nA three piece shower suite with Mira attachment, tiled floor, partly tiled walls and the benefit of built-in storage.\n\n"
